          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: During the night of March 31 to April 1, 2001, and the following night, several witnesses observed a brighter-than-star light point. When viewed through binoculars, color flashes appeared in the light point. The phenomenon made no sound and was observed for several hours. It is likely that these observations were of particularly bright stars.",
